\section*{Unrestricted odd two-adic pro-modularity over Q}

\subsection{OpenAI's claim}
OpenAI presents the following claims relevant to this question, with manuscript numbers following paper order in Sources. In manuscript 1 (family 010; 2026-10-04), the asserted result is that every odd, absolutely irreducible two-dimensional two-adic representation of the rational Galois group with finite ramification occurs in completed Hecke theory at some odd tame level, without a de Rham assumption.

\subsection{Outline of the argument}
For manuscript 1 (family 010; 2026-10-04), a trace family is supplied with potentially automorphic support and a regular point. Coinvariants of local block modules are compared along characteristic-two curves; admissibility and a full adjoint tangent estimate propagate the supporting component back to the original representation.

\subsection{Scope relative to this problem}
The result supplies the conclusion in this problem with its displayed hypotheses and quantifiers. The broader statements and applications in the manuscript are kept separate from the particular question above. The supporting result is manuscript 1 (family 010; 2026-10-04).

\subsection{Formal verification}
